          "english_quote": "So keep purity and reverence, and you will live to God.",
          "issue": "“Reverence” shifts σεμνότητα from dignified moral seriousness in one's conduct to an attitude of profound respect or veneration. The lexical metadata correctly identifies dignified moral seriousness, but that explanation does not make the main-text word communicate the same quality. This is a semantic substitution, not merely a preference for a different register.",
          "suggested_revision": "For fresh review, consider: “So keep purity and dignity, and you will live to God.” Alternatively, consider “purity and dignified seriousness” if “dignity” alone would obscure the ethical sense. Align the lexical rationale and footnote with whichever wording is subsequently approved.",
