          "english_quote": "Keep purity and reverence, and you will live to God.",
          "issue": "Independently against the Greek, “reverence” presents an attitude of respect or veneration rather than the dignified moral seriousness expressed by σεμνότητα here. The simplified edition's metadata explains the intended meaning, but the reader-facing wording still substitutes a different quality.",
          "suggested_revision": "For fresh review, consider: “Keep purity and dignity, and you will live to God.” Another candidate is “Keep purity and seriousness in your conduct, and you will live to God.” Review the latter for its explanatory expansion before adopting it, and update the corresponding metadata.",
